{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And he shall dwell in it until the death of the high priest.</b> So that people would not murmur against the high priest when they see the murderer going out outside the city of his refuge, saying: have you seen this one who killed a soul — he goes out and comes in among people for nothing, and the priest does not take vengeance on him, when the matter is upon him to do, as it is written: והאיש אשר יעשה בזדון לבלתי שמוע אל הכהן וגו׳. But the priest who arises after him — there is nothing to murmur about him over what was not done in his days."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:45.550868930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}